{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Gary Clark Jr. Live felt like a natural next choice because my interest in Hendrix carries over to expressive live blues guitar.",
    "The Breeze felt especially right because Old Sock made the Clapton connection appealing, and relaxed blues is what I want to hear now."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Duets felt less relevant because vocal collaborations do not satisfy my current interest in guitar-focused music.",
    "Led Zeppelin IV and the Beatles retrospective fit my broader interests, but I would rather discover something new today; CSNY 1974 also feels like more listening than I want to commit to."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations leaned too heavily on my broad interest in classic rock, when that alone does not make an album something I would choose now.",
    "Connections to familiar artists seemed to carry too much weight without enough attention to whether I wanted blues guitar, vocal collaborations, or retrospective material."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The appeal of Old Sock and People, Hell & Angels is especially useful for understanding my current preference for relaxed blues and expressive guitar playing.",
    "I rarely choose many items at once: something can fit my taste and still lose out to a stronger immediate choice, as Different Shades Of Blue did today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my rock and blues interests, but my choices today favor guitar-focused blues discoveries over broad classic-rock familiarity."
}"}
